  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Aeluma’s narrative centers on its compound semiconductor photonics platform, positioned to resolve critical supply-chain bottlenecks in AI infrastructure. Current revenue is almost entirely from government R&D contracts, with commercial adoption still in early qualification stages across AI datacom, defense, and sensing applications. Demand tailwinds are strong, but the company remains pre-commercial at scale, making small top-line fluctuations highly amplified in market sentiment. The AI infrastructure buildout provides a powerful secular theme, yet commercialization risk is the dominant uncertainty.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management is steering the business toward commercial production through manufacturing partnerships and qualification processes, while narrowing full-year guidance has been seen by some as a modest miss that masks underlying de-risking progress. The strategy aims to convert a differentiated R&D pipeline into scalable revenue, but execution remains unproven. Credibility is split: bullish narratives highlight a long-term launchpad story, while skeptics note shareholder dilution and the gap between government contract stability and the volatility of an early-stage commercial ramp.",
